  "notes": "A shared context (one Autark node loading the extract's parks and buildings, three code nodes for the heights, the open-air parks and the marked building parts, and three Parameter nodes) feeds three scenarios. Each runs SCOUT's rasterizer and Deep Umbra, measures the shade in each park (rasterio's geometry_mask) and draws its buildings and shadow on Autark maps; Towers removed and Height cap first take out the marked parts or cut them down in a Python node each, by the column around_park. Scout's Dots with a range charts the parks' shade in the three scenarios, and for each what-if a Raster Calculator takes its change in shadow and a Python node, joining on the park's name, its change per park, each drawn by an Autark map after it."
